This is a rust project with crates in the crates dir:
lumina: the main code for lumina, contains all the core logic
lumina-bench: bench marking
lumina-cli: the command line interface, use lumina crate
lumina-mcp: the mcp servers that ship with lumina. the developer sub system is of special interest
lumina-server: the server that supports the desktop (electron) app. also known as luminad


ui/desktop has an electron app in typescript.

non trivial features should be implemented in the lumina crate and then be called from the lumina-cli crate for the cli. for the desktop, you want to add routes to
lumina-server/src/routes. you can then run `just generate-openapi` to generate the openapi spec which will modify the ui/desktop/src/api files. once you have
that you can call the functionality from the server from the typescript.

tips:
- can look at unstaged changes for what is being worked on if starting
- always check rust compiles, cargo fmt etc and `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` (as well as run tests in files you are working on)
- in ui/desktop, look at how you can run lint checks and if other tests can run
